            <ArticleTitle>Juvenile mycosis fungoides with large-cell transformation: Successful treatment with psoralen with ultraviolet A light, interferon-alfa, and localized radiation.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/pde.13338</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mycosis fungoides with large-cell transformation is historically associated with a poor prognosis. Pediatric cases of mycosis fungoides with large-cell transformation are rare, with only three other cases reported in the literature. We present the first case of a child with almost complete remission of his mycosis fungoides with large-cell transformation shortly after administration of psoralen plus ultraviolet A, interferon-alfa, and localized radiation.</AbstractText>
